flowchart TB
    accTitle: What a tap on a player does
    accDescr: Ada plays, and a tap on Bob switches. The extension renews Bob's session at Autodarts with his parked token or, when Autodarts refuses the token, with his remembered password. When that fails, the page stays as it is and no token is lost: Bob has to sign in again when Autodarts refused him, and a tap later tries again when Autodarts couldn't be reached. Otherwise the extension saves Bob's fresh token and renews the session in the page once, to learn whose it is; without an answer, the page stays as it is here too. It parks that session with the account it belongs to, still valid at Autodarts, usually Ada's, writes Bob's session into the page and reloads it, and every other Autodarts tab reloads as Bob.

    tap["Ada plays,<br>a tap on Bob"]
    renew["Renew Bob's session<br>at Autodarts: with his<br>parked token, or with<br>his remembered password<br>when the token is refused"]
    stays["The page stays as it is,<br>no token is lost<br>refused: Bob signs in again<br>no answer: tap again later"]
    save["Save Bob's fresh token"]
    who["Renew the session<br>in the page once:<br>whose is it?"]
    park["Park it with the account<br>it belongs to, usually Ada;<br>it stays valid at Autodarts"]
    write["Write Bob's session<br>into the page, reload it"]
    others["Every other Autodarts tab<br>reloads as Bob"]

    tap --> renew
    renew -- "renewed" --> save
    save --> who
    who -- "Autodarts names<br>the account" --> park
    park --> write --> others
    renew -. "not renewed" .-> stays
    who -. "no answer" .-> stays
    others ~~~ stays

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef failed fill:#dc26262e,stroke:#dc2626,stroke-width:2px
    class tap person
    class renew,save,who,park,write bot
    class others done
    class stays failed
